 that deku has a very special  power a power that is uniquely suited  for defeating all for one that is the  reason why all for one is targeting deku  but it's also the best hope that the  people of japan have in terms of  actually defeating all for one and the  villains ochako tells the crowd to take  a look at deku and the terrible state  that he is in because he has been  working so hard to protect everyone he  kept moving and fighting the villains  tirelessly for days on end even though  he was being targeted by the worst of  the villains and he could have been  killed at any moment several people in  the crowd seem to be finally getting the  message and we see the furry girl that  we met back in chapter 310 as she  recognizes deku as the boy who saved her  as you will recall she was being  attacked by a bunch of hooligans just  because of the way she looked but deku  came and rescued her ochako proclaims  that even though deku has a special  power he is not a special person he is  just a regular guy he's a normal person  like everyone else but he still fights  hard and gives it his all in the name of  protecting others this is what makes  deku a true hero he is not superhuman he  deals with all the same problems and  challenges as everyone else and yet he  still keeps pushing forward for the sake  of others ochako believes that although  taking the first step is always hard  taking this step of actually accepting  deku will lead to the birth of a true  hero a hero who will surpass even all  might deku has the potential to become  the greatest hero the world has ever  known a hero greater than all might but  the people need to take a leap of faith  and believe in him and that is how this  chapter ends by hitting us right in the  fields yet again  and you know what as i am taking in this  conflict between deku's friends and  teachers who are trying to protect him  and the general public who don't want  him anywhere near them i can't help but  think that all might